config UF2_DFU_RESET
	bool "Enable TinyUF2 1200-bps bootloader auto-trigger"
	default y
	help
	  Arms a minimal on-chip USB CDC ACM stack (built on the STM32C5
	  HAL NG PCD API) so that when the host opens the serial port
	  at 1200 baud, the application writes the TinyUF2 DBL_TAP_MAGIC
	  to the top of SRAM and resets into the bootloader.  No manual
	  RESET double-tap required.

	  The STM32C5 HAL NG PCD API is incompatible with Zephyr's USB
	  drivers, so this module provides its own minimal USB CDC ACM
	  implementation and initializes it automatically via SYS_INIT().
